   "notes": "Lion Yard, east-facing buff/yellow stock-brick wall on the small square by St Andrew the Great (west end of St Tibbs Row), next to the granite-pier mall entrance at p0. Plain brick (blue plaque at ~x 2.8) then a full-height white-framed glazed bay (x ~3.9-8.0): ground-floor glazing (advertising panels in 2017), a dark spandrel band and three upper glazed panels up to ~7.9 m; narrow brick return to p1. Read from two near-frontal views (mapillary 242472094330796, 459937365094834)."
